from pathlib import Path
p=Path('README.md')
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
s=s.replace('![Vercel](https://img.shields.io/badge/Hosted_on-Vercel-000000?logo=vercel&logoColor=white)', '![Tailwind CSS 4](https://img.shields.io/badge/Tailwind_CSS-4-06B6D4?logo=tailwindcss&logoColor=white) ![Vercel](https://img.shields.io/badge/Hosted_on-Vercel-000000?logo=vercel&logoColor=white)')
s=s.replace('**This separate adaptation uses React, Vite, JavaScript, and CSS**', '**This separate adaptation uses React, Vite, JavaScript, Tailwind CSS 4, Tailwind Typography, and custom CSS**')
s=s.replace('SapaTamu includes two public-portal screenshots; the other galleries each include three.', 'SapaTamu includes four current public-demo screenshots; the other galleries each include three.')
s=s.replace('| Motion |', '| Typography | Integrated Tailwind CSS 4 through Vite and the official Typography plugin. Shared Prose styles unify biography, project descriptions, and experience bullets; headings balance, paragraphs wrap naturally, and responsive utility classes control grids and spacing. |\n| Motion |')
start=s.index('1. **[SapaTamu - Digital Guestbook]')
end=s.index('\n',start)
s=s[:start]+'1. **[SapaTamu - Digital Guestbook](https://sapatamu-eight.vercel.app/)** — reception dashboard, searchable guest lists, invitations and RSVP, QR check-in, seating plans, meals, souvenirs, gifts, guest wishes, and reporting controls. Next.js and React. Four screenshots were captured directly from the public demo on 27 October 2026; all displayed guest/event information is sample data.'+s[end:]
s=s.replace('- React 19, JavaScript, and Vite 6.', '- React 19, JavaScript, and Vite 6.\n- Tailwind CSS 4 with `@tailwindcss/vite`, plus `@tailwindcss/typography` for shared readable content.\n- Theme-aware Tailwind tokens adapt the existing black/navy and light-mode CSS variables.')
s=s.replace('- CSS variables, responsive layouts, local Plus Jakarta Sans fonts, and SVG icons.', '- CSS variables, responsive utility classes, local Plus Jakarta Sans fonts, and SVG icons.\n- Archived reference layout CSS is no longer loaded; local font declarations are isolated in `fonts.css`.')
s=s.replace('  Replica.jsx          Pages,', '  tailwind.css         Tailwind entry, theme adapter, and Typography colors\n  Prose.jsx            Shared readable paragraphs and lists\n  fonts.css            Local font faces without archived layout rules\n  Replica.jsx          Pages,')
s=s.replace('are reference archives. Their original application scripts and analytics are not executed.', 'are reference archives. Their original layout stylesheet, application scripts, and analytics are not executed. Existing local font files remain in use.')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=Path('DESIGN.md')
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
s+='''\n## Tailwind typography and SapaTamu refresh — 27 October 2026\nThe portfolio remains a brand/content site for recruiters: retain the black/navy identity, Plus Jakarta Sans, original portrait reveal, and Enji credit. Tailwind CSS 4 runs through @tailwindcss/vite; the official Typography plugin and shared Prose.jsx own long-form rhythm. Body copy is 15px on phones / 16px from 640px with 1.8 line height; narrative blocks use 65–68ch maximum widths, headings use balance, and paragraphs use pretty wrapping. Feature lists use one column on phones and two from 640px. Runtime CSS variables in replica.css remain canonical (Model B): --page-bg, --surface, --surface-hover, --line, --text, --muted, --accent map to Tailwind page/panel/panel-hover/divider/ink/soft/highlight via @theme inline. Typography colors adapt these same variables; theme changes do not duplicate palettes. Custom layout rules live in the components layer, below utility classes; motion.css retains bespoke SVG effects. Archived reference layout CSS is no longer loaded: fonts.css contains only the existing local Jakarta font declarations.\nSapaTamu now exposes a public demo. Four current screenshots show summary, guest list, QR check-in reception, and seating plan with fictional event data. The gallery preserves the screenshots' 1526/635 aspect ratio. Feature copy describes visible workflow modules; no real guest records or personal account credentials are published.\n\n| Maintained rule | Runtime evidence | Migration decision |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Preserve original layout and motion | Replica.jsx, contents.css, Motion.jsx | Keep custom components and motion; Tailwind handles shared text and responsive grids. |\n| Local fonts | fonts.css and existing local woff2 files | Stop loading archived layout CSS to remove conflicting resets. |\n| Honest project screenshots | portfolio-data.js and SapaTamu public demo | Replace login/recovery slides with four actual dashboard/workflow captures. |\n'''
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=Path('app/AGENTS.md')
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
s+='\nTailwind CSS 4 is integrated with @tailwindcss/vite and @tailwindcss/typography. Use shared Prose.jsx for narrative copy and CV bullets; use theme-adapted utilities from tailwind.css. Keep custom styles in the components layer so utilities have a predictable cascade. fonts.css loads local Plus Jakarta Sans; do not restore the archived layout stylesheet in index.html. SapaTamu gallery now uses four current public-demo screenshots (summary, guests, check-in, seating); all shown data is fictional. Preserve screenshot aspect ratio and the existing theme/Focus/TOC behaviors.\n'
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
